<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ishaq ibn Muhammad ibn Ghaniya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1183</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ishaq ibn Muhammad ibn Ghaniya was emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mallorca">Majorca</a> from about 1155 to 1183, the leading ruler of the Banu Ghaniya, a branch of the Almoravid family that kept the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balearic-islands">Balearic Islands</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a> collapsed. Under him Majorca prospered from trade and corsair raids, and he made treaties with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pisa">Pisa</a>. His sons, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-ibn-ghaniya">Ali ibn Ghaniya</a>, invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> in 1184 to fight the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohads</a>.</p></div>
